# Harr host adapter: OpenCode is native-first (like ZCode). The LeanCTX MCP stays
# registered for CodeGraph, the service MCPs and named Ein; CTX_* entries name the
# primary tool for each shared routing rule, not necessarily a LeanCTX tool id.
CTX_READ='native read'
CTX_SHELL='lean-ctx_ctx_shell'
CTX_SEARCH='native grep'
CTX_GLOB='native glob'
CTX_TOOLS='lean-ctx_ctx_tools'
CTX_CALL='lean-ctx_ctx_call'
HOST_ORCHESTRATION_POLICY=''
HOST_NATIVE_POLICY='OpenCode native-first routing: native read/grep/glob inspect exact source and the native editor makes edits. Shell work goes through lean-ctx_ctx_shell. LeanCTX offers only ctx_shell for bounded commands, ctx_tools for CodeGraph/service MCPs, and ctx_call solely to recover an archived shell result via name=ctx_expand and its returned id. Treat a CodeGraph or compressed overview as navigation, never as proof of behavior; confirm branches, error paths, ordering, ownership and edge cases in exact source before editing or asserting conclusions. Do not re-read identical exact source without a concrete reason; keep queries and line windows narrow. If shell output is archived, use ctx_call(name=ctx_expand, arguments={id: <returned archive id>, ...narrow selector}) for only the needed evidence. Do not use ctx_call for ordinary file reading, search, edits or shell work. Do not guess truncated results or silently bypass the shell policy.'
